docs/DECISIONS-log.md:1689:- The window: "嗯改成 8/15 吧；然后已有的结果封存，然后改一下重判的设置，然后继续跑完剩下的". The results through the last completed day are sealed in `poc/data/sealed-2026-10-24-run3-through-0728/` with `SHA256SUMS`; the same views database continues from the next day to 2026-08-15 with daily re-judging.
docs/DECISIONS-log.md:2321:- Validation is on real data, not the three-article experiments: the seed, then the week 2026-07-24..27 on `poc/data/english-groups2-2026-10-25/`, read group by group (Rubin shipment with its customer deployments; the OpenAI–NVIDIA financing and Ohio campus; the hyperscaler capex cycle; China chip export controls; PC and other companies' own lines outside those). Alex: stop and report as soon as the groups look wrong ("如果你跑了前几天就发现grouping 有问题或是实现出来的质量有问题就停止来和我说").
docs/DECISIONS-log.md:2328:- Validation stays small: the seed and the first two week days on a fresh ledger (`poc/data/english-groups3-2026-10-25/`, poc-v21), read group by group before anything larger.
docs/DECISIONS-log.md:2498:- Decided to build and run alone: `matching` keeps Jev; a configuration may add a `collision` setting (model, prompt `collision-v1`). When a candidate's list holds a thesis of its own object and measure, one generative call answers the analyst question for those theses and its verdict replaces Jev's on them (`jev_matching.collision_peers`, `ask_collision_judge`); every other relation stays Jev's. `poc-v26` = `poc-v25` plus the judge. Measured by one run over seed, week and August against the extraction gold and the census (ledger `english-v26-collision-r4-2026-10-26`); result appended here.
docs/DECISIONS-log.md:2620:- Found in the three-month resume (`english-v34-nvda-3m-2026-10-28`, 01:32): the judgement of v10 (Data Center revenue, a 24,150-token request) came back empty with `finish_reason` length: all 8,000 completion tokens were reasoning tokens, so the code read a malformed answer and the day halted (resumable; the re-send passed). Census over every archive: 2 of 793 judge answers hit the cap this way (the other in `english-v29-nvda-3m`, a 56k-token request), 13 of 793 used 6,000 or more. The archive books such a call at $0 while it costs its tokens (about $0.006 each).
docs/DECISIONS-log.md:3792:- The run (`english-v34-nvda-3m-2026-10-28`, poc-v34, the D202–D205 writer) completed 59 days, 2026-07-01 to 08-28: 1,232 items, 69 theses, 7,091 calls, $5.80. It is sealed read-only as `poc/data/sealed-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/` (SQLite online backups, SHA256SUMS, logs and scripts; the run folder is left resumable). The front end reads it from 16:35: the served defaults switched in the five places the README names (main checkout), `poc/mock/index.html` rebuilt, the API restarted in `service-3m-2026-10-28/` (`/days` 2026-07-01..08-28, 69 theses).

