  1676	## D62 · 2026-10-23 · The POC build: Alex's choices, in his words
  1677	
  1678	- Build started on the frozen design (2026-10-23): "数据准备好了之后，你清洗干净就可以准备开始去建这个 POC 的管线", "尽量按照那个系统设计来……当然没有这么复杂……做简洁一点". The simplifications are listed in `docs/poc/pipeline-plan.md`; nothing in the frozen PRDs changed.
  1679	- No cap on the number of views: "不一定要二到四个问题啊". The model decides; code checks only the shape (ladder, due day, quarter, year).
  1680	- The corpus first, whole and original: "先建好这个素材库……再尝试来建构这个管线"; "要像是原始数据……不能是你自己已经处理过的". Industry, macro, geopolitics and noise added: "起码多两倍的数据".
  1681	- Test small before any full run: "你最好小范围的测试下不要全部跑完然后完全不 work 或是质量有问题再全部重跑". The first week, then August: "你别全跑，到 8 月底先。我们来完整的看下结果".
  1682	- Extraction variance is fixed in the prompt, not by sampling several times: "太浪费钱和时间了，那你的 prompt 就应该改成可以抽的出来的方式". The v2 extraction prompt replaces taste words and the company-specific line with rules checkable against the material (the firm's total and largest-segment full-year numbers, every full-year number the firm guides, dated pending events); measured on the same transcript three times, the core set is stable (`docs/poc/pipeline-plan.md`).
  1683	- Model: gpt-6-luna stays: "那我觉得还是用 luna 吧，记录这个比较结果". The comparison with DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017 (the `deepseek-flash` endpoint) is in `docs/poc/pipeline-plan.md`: the only way to get schema-valid JSON from it was a strict tool call with thinking off (3/3; json_object 2/3 and 1/3; thinking-mode forbids a forced tool_choice); about five times cheaper (≈$0.01 against ≈$0.05 per transcript), 18–22 s against 26–31 s, three times more evidence, the candidate set a little less stable; matching and re-judging were not tested on it.
  1684	
  1685	## D63 · 2026-10-24 · Re-judging once a day; the first window ends on 2026-08-15
  1686	
  1687	- Alex, shown that re-judging was half the cost (a hot view re-judged after every item, each call carrying all its evidence): "是的应该要一天一次". Re-judging moves from each item's round to one round per day: the day's items are extracted, matched and written in sequence as before; after the last item, and before pull mode freezes the views due that day, one judging round runs over every open view whose reading changed that day, dependencies first, each view once, dependants added when a dependency's conclusion changed. The judgement is recorded under the day's own processing record (`day:<date>`) at the day's last sequence number. This amends 06-views step 7 / D51 for the POC; the design text is updated when Alex takes the module up. The stream still never reads the calendar: the day comes from the replay (in production, from pull mode).
  1688	- Reasoning effort stays medium: "可以之后试试看比较质量，这次先别改".
  1689	- The window: "嗯改成 8/15 吧；然后已有的结果封存，然后改一下重判的设置，然后继续跑完剩下的". The results through the last completed day are sealed in `poc/data/sealed-2026-10-24-run3-through-0728/` with `SHA256SUMS`; the same views database continues from the next day to 2026-08-15 with daily re-judging.
  3790	
  3791	- Alex, 16:30: "你先停止吧，把这个db 封存，替换成最新的FE可以读取然后把这个 bloating evidence 的问题给记录下来，很严重，需要解决". Earlier (16:12): "证据膨胀是一个问题，我们之后要想办法deal".
  3792	- The run (`english-v34-nvda-3m-2026-10-28`, poc-v34, the D202–D205 writer) completed 59 days, 2026-07-01 to 08-28: 1,232 items, 69 theses, 7,091 calls, $5.80. It is sealed read-only as `poc/data/sealed-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/` (SQLite online backups, SHA256SUMS, logs and scripts; the run folder is left resumable). The front end reads it from 16:35: the served defaults switched in the five places the README names (main checkout), `poc/mock/index.html` rebuilt, the API restarted in `service-3m-2026-10-28/` (`/days` 2026-07-01..08-28, 69 theses).
  3793	- Why it stops: evidence bloat. The Data Center revenue thesis (v10) carried 1,768 linked pieces by 08-27 and FY2027 revenue (v2) 1,733; v10's judging request was 292 KB with 698 evidence ids shown; the model mislabels one id among dozens of pushes about every other attempt, the code refuses the answer, two refusals halt the day. Today: 14 judge answers refused by code, 10 on v10/v2/v13, two days halted on v10 alone in 16:05–16:21. Of 25 pieces linked to v2, 10 bear on the question (Claude's reading); the judge ever cited 23–27% of what is linked. The census, the one-case traces and the rule candidates are in `docs/research/2026-10-28-quality-review/report.md` §2 D (and A–C, measured first); the step is Alex's to pick.
