# Sealed: the three-month NVDA run under poc-v34 (extraction v18, D202–D205 writer), 2026-07-01 to 2026-08-28

Stopped by Alex on 2026-10-28 16:30 after 59 completed days ("你先停止吧，把这个db 封存"): evidence bloat made the
Data Center revenue thesis's judgement fail about every other attempt (quality review §2 D). 1,232 items handed over,
69 theses, 7,091 archived calls, $5.80. `views.sqlite` and `archive.sqlite` are SQLite online backups of the run folder
`english-v34-nvda-3m-2026-10-28/` (left resumable, untouched). Read-only; checksums in SHA256SUMS.
Served to the front end from 2026-10-28 (scripts/hivemind_api.py --views …/sealed-…/views.sqlite).
poc/data/served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/README.md
# Served copy of the sealed 2026-10-28 ledger, minus v68

`views.sqlite` = `sealed-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite` with thesis v68 removed (Alex, 2026-10-28 17:05:
"你直接把它移除，这是我们自己的失误"). v68, "What stand-alone CPU revenue will NVIDIA report for calendar 2027?", was opened on the
run's last day by the succession rule (same quantity, next period, after v24) and the writer linked its one opening statement to
v7 and v24 instead of to it, so it stood with no evidence and no judgement. Rows removed: views, view_keys, rungs, successions,
view_switches, views_fts for v68 (no evidence_links or judgements existed). The sealed folder is untouched and remains the record;
the front end, the API and the page build read this copy.
